    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="19" relname="span">We have all made decisions based on our intuition.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="20" relname="span">Without reason or cause we knew that the direction we were about to take was the right one or the wrong one.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="elaboration">It was a feeling that had no basis what so ever.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="21" relname="span">Intuitiveness also has its place in interface design.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="18" relname="span">The term intuitive, however, means different things to different users.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="elaboration">To some it means an intuitive user interface is one that users can figure out on their own,</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="17" relname="span">but to Chris Brown (1995) an intuitive user interface in one that is easy to learn.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="23" relname="antithesis">This does not mean that no instruction is required,</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="23" relname="span">but it is minimal,</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="9" relname="elaboration">making it easy for users to pick up and remember.</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="25" relname="span">Intuitiveness can be assessed by measuring the products learnability or familiarity.</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="26" relname="span">In other words, how quickly the products usage was grasped by initial users (Bacon, 2004).</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="27" relname="span">Usability testing serves well in this capacity.</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="13" relname="means">By using various verbal instructions researchers can test their interfaces on inexperienced users and determine its ease of use and learnability.</segment>
        <group id="15" type="multinuc"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="15" relname="joint"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="24" relname="span"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="4" relname="background"/>
